#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179602 :question/id #uuid "6c8b136c-7944-599f-9399-19641212fcbe" :question/math-academy-id "e-9537" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7e61f72ed7488fd490f42ff519316ed2e87d3c997d64e2cc6b7af36f951dbb5.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $\\mathbf F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r =  0\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r > 0\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r > 0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $\\Gamma$ measures the total work done by a force $\\mathbf F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\Gamma = \\oint\\limits_C \\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm{d} \\mathbf r\n= \\int_a^b \\mathbf F(r(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf r'(t) \\; \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r > 0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r <                               0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Since the force $\\mathbf F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves around $C,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/06/063836a4780ecb4be6e8c6149a422e3c8e9f2770304e659a8116691b91e3d7f1.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $\\mathbf F$ remains unchanged.\n\n![](images/70/704915d2852e1654aa31d17bd2dfb07a3022fe3d8b597f37bf98bd5af2de1d1b.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179603 :question/id #uuid "16605c7c-c238-51ef-84e6-d5b5d58e1539" :question/math-academy-id "e-9539" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y) = -y\\,\\mathbf{i} +x\\,\\mathbf{j}$ along the circle $C$ with equation $x^2 + y^2 = 1,$ oriented counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "The closed curve $C$ is the unit circle. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\cos{t}\\,\\mathbf{i} + \\sin{t}\\,\\mathbf{j},\n\\qquad 0 \\leq t \\lt 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nThe circulation $\\Gamma$ measures the total work done by a force $\\mathbf F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\Gamma = \\oint\\limits_C \\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm{d} \\mathbf r\n= \\int_a^b \\mathbf F(r(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf r'(t) \\; \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx = \\cos t, \\qquad\ny = \\sin t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))=-y\\,i+x\\,j=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r'(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179605 :question/id #uuid "1e15ae93-0a63-506a-a0ae-b15e035f0494" :question/math-academy-id "e-9543" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y) =( e^y+x)\\,\\mathbf i +(xe^y+y^2)\\,\\mathbf j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathbf F$ is conservative\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_C\\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm d\\mathbf r = 0\n$$ for any piecewise-smooth path $C\\in\\mathbb R^2$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle\\oint\\limits_C\\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm d\\mathbf r =0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in\\mathbb R^2$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf F$ is a conservative vector field on $\\mathbb R^2,$ then the circulation $\\Gamma = 0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in\\mathbb R^2,$ that is \n\n$$\n\\Gamma = \\oint\\limits_C \\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm{d} \\mathbf r = 0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $\\mathbf F = P\\,\\mathbf i + Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is a vector field with domain $D = \\mathbb R^2.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} =  e^y.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $\\mathbf F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on $\\mathbb R^2.$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. The result $\\Gamma = 0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "493ec38d-6098-515e-a5ad-7028e14e4279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369286} {:answer/id #uuid "60467e75-9aeb-5f89-b5ba-0cf99f9bee14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-50\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369287} {:answer/id #uuid "b63af696-8674-5081-a959-eef7b89a95b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369288} {:answer/id #uuid "75a9f5c7-a760-53e9-ad0a-e67425e54722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369289} {:answer/id #uuid "d22cce2e-96a1-5175-b7a3-60ee2d75ac84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60467e75-9aeb-5f89-b5ba-0cf99f9bee14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-50\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369287} :answer-field/id #uuid "caad0ef3-4ef7-5f6c-a0d6-18c2861ca703" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "122d93a7-8517-5ac5-b32a-6a8ca24b241f" :question/math-academy-id "q-125393" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=y\\,i-x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i-x\\,j \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-25{sin}^{2}⁡t-25{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-25)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-25t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-25(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-50\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a2d901-52dc-580c-b53b-e7be3980d2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459485} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd85d8b-be1b-575e-80ac-713251f2e060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07a2d901-52dc-580c-b53b-e7be3980d2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459485} :answer-field/id #uuid "68a91996-588b-523d-920f-19a0c8f2360d" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460609} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "445c0216-e1b1-5dd3-8feb-cc822c3d9a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459487} {:answer/id #uuid "17e40de4-f646-5021-9351-81097f6cd6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17e40de4-f646-5021-9351-81097f6cd6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459488} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5092c7-0f51-5842-8bc5-c41ed85755e5" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a377412f-eec0-5aeb-b5a0-47d4b28ce15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459489} {:answer/id #uuid "872e5857-37ec-5931-83c9-83ec8a9ea82a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a377412f-eec0-5aeb-b5a0-47d4b28ce15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459489} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe9a2195-fa09-5aad-adbc-06b68d958d2b" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1d320327-1d15-55df-b5dd-771fb0fd1831" :question/math-academy-id "q-125394" :question/problem "![](images/27/270e72ebedac3741e1b7086021b16dc0975ae9852d402673c8044a67f8f774fb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/db/dbb6dbdfabccf7a94c67781210238c647e6f3a2e428cb79c4debdbff5e124720.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/1c/1c5aa77b0a89e1fcb0782c9d969d3a81bbec47b004f07bd3a53ccd10e623ba6e.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8b6878-85b8-58eb-a242-cf54f14a0ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459491} {:answer/id #uuid "31fb75c7-a022-54df-a901-a9869c56eff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8b6878-85b8-58eb-a242-cf54f14a0ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459491} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e67b26d-312f-5124-b515-45ca803fdb86" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460612} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "310240c9-bca3-503f-87c1-b88b9a790c48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459493} {:answer/id #uuid "8acc9467-c049-5e2f-91a7-f70e0c1b40fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "310240c9-bca3-503f-87c1-b88b9a790c48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459493} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a84f387-e198-5acc-ae65-f1896114917e" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9fa6a11-4b01-5ec8-98ee-ef928f01c5a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459495} {:answer/id #uuid "aefb95da-9bcd-543a-8c79-cce66b4132ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aefb95da-9bcd-543a-8c79-cce66b4132ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459496} :answer-field/id #uuid "c520ba73-5e23-574e-b441-acfbad776311" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "889fbef5-9dc3-5991-a476-ffe3c0711611" :question/math-academy-id "q-125395" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0ae64bf57444ac42ec5efed392471cbbac7b1e317bc1fb06b33bcd2038a2e3c1.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ are false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/bc/bc0121782b16d513d7d17d3741bd07ef1716e096bb2459fbda0cb841c7fd8b43.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $-C.$\n\n![](images/1a/1a6b109bc1da3aa7905b05f7f7902523b45fd51a65b97bec1328037bd6c0cfe7.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f564f77-c024-5353-a9d9-c19914097692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459503} {:answer/id #uuid "660514de-f28c-53cb-a27c-34d751510c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "660514de-f28c-53cb-a27c-34d751510c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459504} :answer-field/id #uuid "edfbdfc1-8a04-5a73-afb3-039c7c9d5bc1" :answer-field/key "$∇f$ is conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460618} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39b0f616-1749-542e-b105-fe3297acb197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459505} {:answer/id #uuid "39f55c24-bf0b-53af-ba47-2beb4d0758c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39f55c24-bf0b-53af-ba47-2beb4d0758c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459506} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e7a67e4-edf9-59f3-a000-81656a4d6fc4" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33539880-33d2-58c3-8020-27c2bed37c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459507} {:answer/id #uuid "20852a9c-f055-5c0a-9c0b-3b8d3eff6c12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33539880-33d2-58c3-8020-27c2bed37c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459507} :answer-field/id #uuid "80bbfcb7-86eb-5f41-a1ce-925daa85ec41" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460620} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ea644c1-0089-5ce6-9c36-851f16684cb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667914} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7eefa9-0544-5a49-95ea-35c04ebfb56c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ea644c1-0089-5ce6-9c36-851f16684cb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667914} :answer-field/id #uuid "0697e6d0-3d3e-5782-af58-1eb3c156fa23" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "76c1a939-3dff-51ed-a845-c6333747802b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125424" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$∇f$ is conservative” is true. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is true, while statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∇f$ is conservative”; “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c797ef94-90e6-566b-9b43-0bf4ebfc0174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448182} {:answer/id #uuid "2108e7ba-2d02-5d40-ad7b-b6dc5ede1dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2108e7ba-2d02-5d40-ad7b-b6dc5ede1dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448183} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e7c442-37b4-53e5-9361-ab0e0727c669" :answer-field/key "$F$ is conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe589362-8c90-5180-9570-91a94c008ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448184} {:answer/id #uuid "f3810666-82a6-5190-a96d-b72a05c69e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe589362-8c90-5180-9570-91a94c008ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448184} :answer-field/id #uuid "09b47f93-aa6a-5f17-afba-163dad61d2d3" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449132} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57eeac5b-df12-5620-9756-7c63284a2ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448186} {:answer/id #uuid "946432ba-9af2-53d8-8a78-d7ff15949612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "946432ba-9af2-53d8-8a78-d7ff15949612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448187} :answer-field/id #uuid "2424a3b9-022b-501a-bc4b-da6b53737e91" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dfac5beb-f3c0-5ece-80d7-1d1e280a780f" :question/math-academy-id "q-125432" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y)=-\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{2y}{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j.\n$$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4xy}{(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$F$ is conservative” is true. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false, while statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$F$ is conservative”; “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20b9603d-bac9-510b-8adf-4811f7de36f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257050} {:answer/id #uuid "26ec99ce-8a59-5b3e-a5e2-b2a4376ef85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257119} {:answer/id #uuid "35ecf7ed-f11b-5da5-add8-dae837fcadb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257256} {:answer/id #uuid "583e6e7c-9d42-5175-a79d-4384af96a328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257546} {:answer/id #uuid "e914a80c-0913-59c3-b9ed-6b86107e11f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ec99ce-8a59-5b3e-a5e2-b2a4376ef85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257119} :answer-field/id #uuid "c32e678d-b7b8-57d6-98b9-3d11c1c55626" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "81113ee4-2843-5316-a3de-8f3bdbd20c2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125485" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation $25{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25$ oriented counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our curve as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThe closed curve $C$ is the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $1$ and $5,$ respectively. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{5}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-1+5 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =4(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =8\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb212b19-0efe-5595-8a6e-e47cc9adaa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462175} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6f84f1-683f-5d00-9604-34d4790cb9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb212b19-0efe-5595-8a6e-e47cc9adaa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462175} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a39db3-475c-5e0a-801d-11e7e55a57ab" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffe3f7d-d217-5537-9b72-5552de904647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462177} {:answer/id #uuid "0df6588a-1243-5256-a273-81f127138027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0df6588a-1243-5256-a273-81f127138027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462178} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8dffca-0ed9-5da1-995f-1364b3fbea05" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ca2cc7-24f7-507a-9285-aa88fa019e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462179} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea2a08c-0d10-592a-9aa9-d6c47c1f74d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32ca2cc7-24f7-507a-9285-aa88fa019e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462179} :answer-field/id #uuid "68723449-ccac-55e8-b16a-59ae779fc661" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4fa44014-b4ce-590d-a5cb-5c0b5e464aaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-125392" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dca985dc352c45477dbb6ada86ad5a9cfa4404969510191a1955e59b082709fe.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves around $C,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/eb/eb4da8143700c7d31e0ceacd09ac76a8d1bcb10379a34dce5b59d48f2ae58c13.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ remains unchanged.\n\n![](images/70/70a473397216589350f63482ab3e36cb1247e7825046c70642254c8514564b00.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1302b599-2239-505b-b3d3-593cd0e7a043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256954} {:answer/id #uuid "25f5a68d-02d4-5d0d-9b6e-50318dfb916d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257107} {:answer/id #uuid "370ef85f-d49d-51a9-b02b-e65db313b71d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257265} {:answer/id #uuid "74c350ba-8dd4-599c-b29b-6c00e2ac65a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257804} {:answer/id #uuid "f2983f61-da9d-57ce-96a7-e897a8003fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "370ef85f-d49d-51a9-b02b-e65db313b71d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257265} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8dc2f8e-7c62-5163-bb3d-95682d8d786c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8861d081-ecb1-543c-9f19-c7f5c4a0eab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-125446" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=-y\\,i+x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =-y\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =2{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "590a9072-3394-532b-a5a0-dc5f49b25f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257555} {:answer/id #uuid "5e4a844c-c7fa-5967-8a71-4a23cafb35dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257609} {:answer/id #uuid "878f3872-5ea2-514f-b1fd-e429a62b2e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257968} {:answer/id #uuid "a47316a6-f4ef-5c35-b6df-f442c5ac4c7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258218} {:answer/id #uuid "f7994ada-b57a-50c5-8da3-ca283cecf0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a47316a6-f4ef-5c35-b6df-f442c5ac4c7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258218} :answer-field/id #uuid "6199c37f-2024-560d-965e-527c92de8df5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c33250ca-91bb-5b15-bb01-0f4acbe13913" :question/math-academy-id "q-125451" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=y\\,i-x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i-x\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}{sin}^{2}⁡t-\\sqrt{3}{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-\\sqrt{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d33e2ea-8db6-5ef9-af39-e635cdeedbe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256910} {:answer/id #uuid "33f16301-edab-5602-af96-594f309388a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257243} {:answer/id #uuid "5acaa948-bf60-5767-bf30-561cf7b9dcff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257572} {:answer/id #uuid "8c32b999-d035-5352-94f4-6157ae6afeb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258012} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cefd61-28ba-5230-bf98-2ca2309bbaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33f16301-edab-5602-af96-594f309388a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257243} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1c0cb9-e215-5ac0-86e2-2c6dc53f7d21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "38a18171-ca9d-5700-9d3e-85fd0dad7304" :question/math-academy-id "q-125455" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=x\\,i+y\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+y\\,j \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\left(\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}\\right)\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(-1+1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc4db62-7cbb-550f-910e-a6df196bd951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256915} {:answer/id #uuid "687be8c6-45bb-5313-80d4-2341b5044e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257708} {:answer/id #uuid "795f43a3-87f8-5cc9-8ea5-d38c6ce4f4c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257855} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3f5190-f7d2-50c3-bc33-b552201b3177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258015} {:answer/id #uuid "cffb7f8a-fef2-56bc-bae5-f715c9c300a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cffb7f8a-fef2-56bc-bae5-f715c9c300a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258585} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5d048a0-23c3-54b5-aed7-75189d8dfd89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6c9b62b5-a1f8-55a4-80ed-a407fed4aa46" :question/math-academy-id "q-125457" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{y}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\left(-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\right)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-2(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44d8a328-aac8-5002-8d62-aef641d7ed52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257384} {:answer/id #uuid "5c930330-229b-51df-b7b9-7c2254d5dae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257586} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe0605a-7ab9-5d75-a8fa-5610e3c0a59c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257919} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0c33dc-0b9b-5290-a327-91d4c7ae1173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258164} {:answer/id #uuid "c284997b-574a-5331-a2d3-a245c6ac66b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fe0605a-7ab9-5d75-a8fa-5610e3c0a59c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257919} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f1aca3d-3380-50cc-afee-7ab8f1d2604f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ddfc51b2-914e-5bd0-b3a5-3b62847ab125" :question/math-academy-id "q-125460" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }10\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =10t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =10(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =20\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37f44aac-0775-51da-a8c4-dfe7f092aa84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257274} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3d44ff-6ba4-5561-aab3-b14b7d6bc9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258014} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e19bb9-c4fe-5782-9083-dfe133debc1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258264} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ba4ba4-edf7-5f3f-bdb9-f225398b9147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258321} {:answer/id #uuid "d04d9343-8b1e-53d0-82f6-5c60b51e7eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0ba4ba4-edf7-5f3f-bdb9-f225398b9147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258321} :answer-field/id #uuid "50d05e08-dfe6-58de-ae50-7ffb1990e442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "205601cc-6f43-54e3-8d21-d33b726485ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-125585" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{3}{y}\\,i-\\frac{2}{x}\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36$ oriented counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our curve as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThe closed curve $C$ is the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $2$ and $3,$ respectively. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{3}{y}\\,i-\\frac{2}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-2-3 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-5)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-5t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-5(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-10\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a074685c-6f81-5431-86de-5f20c4658e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463488} {:answer/id #uuid "24e36323-76da-51e5-bfb2-592610002fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24e36323-76da-51e5-bfb2-592610002fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463489} :answer-field/id #uuid "c743c6e7-059d-5909-9335-e5ad04088599" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464678} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6209e29c-6f4f-5cd2-b854-a9a719c264fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463490} {:answer/id #uuid "a906d4ee-e6aa-54de-9527-ace41765eb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a906d4ee-e6aa-54de-9527-ace41765eb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463491} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fdabed2-ee70-5863-b4f7-2f54d7e967e7" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13acff26-2b2e-5369-9c05-1a4ae2971db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463492} {:answer/id #uuid "21155136-2b73-54fb-aa55-8041c9107e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13acff26-2b2e-5369-9c05-1a4ae2971db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463492} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d92b4b5-1cec-55de-8dcb-2ff6ec78d476" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "547c79d0-6e8c-5db1-9245-a09abf6b78b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-125637" :question/problem "![](images/e6/e60f7c0adc3e2ec8daa3203564c31bf660e6eca7e6394955cc73133ac3673ed5.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is true, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/a8/a8010db8481768cb61d0734dcfc97eed646441ab265c4928d06d274ef0e1c1dd.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $C.$\n\n![](images/be/be263d706bfc3ef205be37aaed85d4984d3739d53cdaadb8cba88e3d5196ce93.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0;\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9988e87b-8bb7-5f6a-8c19-1f86b1e3bec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463494} {:answer/id #uuid "ead72610-955b-5f0a-a542-876b5f86cecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ead72610-955b-5f0a-a542-876b5f86cecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463495} :answer-field/id #uuid "b21e8731-a185-5af2-9809-992523279b8c" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464681} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5478153-7791-5077-b3ce-72c90e76c652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463496} {:answer/id #uuid "0cd852aa-110e-5536-94a1-9cf26cf387f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5478153-7791-5077-b3ce-72c90e76c652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463496} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ac6e374-6544-5656-898d-3dc8a4a1e808" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7839e1e-cae3-5b91-84f5-3ede7feb4f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463498} {:answer/id #uuid "2ae3bf11-7cea-56bb-9911-0dfdd41c3bf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7839e1e-cae3-5b91-84f5-3ede7feb4f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463498} :answer-field/id #uuid "c483a0c2-4150-5b6a-aaca-08fee470ac4d" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "982dcf8b-4c96-5db9-9ec4-1bcce43696b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-125643" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f4042d4eb43310480f3c75673befbf58067a89704d20b9a63f0f6c7272179f3e.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ are false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/fa/fabbbb78d8fd4d327fe82d1d93d8e0fc15dd33e909266e0ef88de931be28b951.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $C.$\n\n![](images/71/712564e3b0ad0e23d2d9097eb02c0857130bdaa6619a005738205130ab66ac3a.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5d80f62-7611-5589-bb35-f2bd8dd2ac54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448188} {:answer/id #uuid "ceba6fca-85bb-5f5b-b472-da4e26311629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceba6fca-85bb-5f5b-b472-da4e26311629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448189} :answer-field/id #uuid "c16dc663-73ea-51dc-bd73-3fce8f2608a4" :answer-field/key "$∇f$ is conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d66252c-0a79-586a-9a03-83c0f08ea4c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448190} {:answer/id #uuid "068689c6-ba01-5b3f-8861-81453ed7f373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d66252c-0a79-586a-9a03-83c0f08ea4c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448190} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c337a6b-db58-56f1-8586-a438e958e686" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449135} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0583a8b5-3c5d-55d5-9ab8-38e4dbed7c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448192} {:answer/id #uuid "0e840e72-c567-58eb-8d86-b77eb69e1aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e840e72-c567-58eb-8d86-b77eb69e1aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448193} :answer-field/id #uuid "94fc3bec-7574-5b7d-9315-47b094cd5a5b" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7b7ddac2-e3bd-590b-a396-56e8108da7f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125647" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$∇f$ is conservative” is true. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false, while statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∇f$ is conservative”; “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc049f21-a499-5e1c-bdab-1491bf8bd7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448194} {:answer/id #uuid "70dba20a-9283-5a64-92e1-e818bbe45555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc049f21-a499-5e1c-bdab-1491bf8bd7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448194} :answer-field/id #uuid "74956c98-32c5-5a81-9fd6-d30967d81c85" :answer-field/key "$∇f$ is **not** conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7320a730-56b8-5dc9-935e-a931fcfdca97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448196} {:answer/id #uuid "14225c91-d53e-564c-a75b-2ff3a307db5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7320a730-56b8-5dc9-935e-a931fcfdca97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448196} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4650f15-3ab9-5cbb-8a44-4f88d6ffeef2" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise linear path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080320d7-6a08-5185-be7b-bf365f7873d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448198} {:answer/id #uuid "556f08e3-7136-594b-bdbf-c1887d7ea54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "556f08e3-7136-594b-bdbf-c1887d7ea54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448199} :answer-field/id #uuid "aff3da6e-b916-5bbe-aee8-f8bb72ec84cd" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "78e40fa2-e07f-5983-b8b1-ed694102f21b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125648" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)={e}^{y}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$∇f$ is **not** conservative” is false. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any piecewise linear path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false, while statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d433da7b-1e1e-535b-9f25-83bdf23e4df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463500} {:answer/id #uuid "b9260be8-c900-5ecd-a29b-b1b5e76ddea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9260be8-c900-5ecd-a29b-b1b5e76ddea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463501} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f88a2a7-6b38-5992-98ee-3c8c44386624" :answer-field/key "$∇f$ is conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbb4515b-adce-511f-9f3e-7963532589f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463502} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0d50d9-8f3d-5d9f-b4f7-523d73146916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbb4515b-adce-511f-9f3e-7963532589f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463502} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7d2d666-5099-5d29-a783-b3acfcfc73d6" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79a18ac3-3da5-5858-a2ae-9bb8d620bf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/i