answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463523} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa9dff9-ff4d-597d-8ef9-69284d5d1e3f" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69d3df83-92d2-5184-b675-b6a5c3c18aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667922} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6cf91a-81b7-5496-9df1-104d1cfe81a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69d3df83-92d2-5184-b675-b6a5c3c18aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667922} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d1a290b-e2a2-5929-b0ab-5562df71eb45" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2353653c-eb1d-5d31-b3c0-eed1015199de" :question/math-academy-id "q-125664" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=({y}^{2}+3x)\\,i+(2xy+3)\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2y.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$F$ is conservative” is true. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$” and “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” are true. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$F$ is conservative”; “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$”; “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06dbf44c-a97d-5504-aaf1-6c264e0b1a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463524} {:answer/id #uuid "8e129735-2b0e-5398-b43e-eba53f0bd641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06dbf44c-a97d-5504-aaf1-6c264e0b1a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463524} :answer-field/id #uuid "c82c86ec-d6d5-5ab6-aee9-a9658eb3f2ee" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ec4d98-ca2c-51aa-a554-0a0261babe64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463526} {:answer/id #uuid "924c827f-ee30-5f0f-9c24-3aa92a243a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16ec4d98-ca2c-51aa-a554-0a0261babe64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463526} :answer-field/id #uuid "936072da-8823-5ffd-a2dc-d329a5e7d650" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aacbbfa5-1cb5-59f3-8092-856333260916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463528} {:answer/id #uuid "e0541a8e-593e-5a77-bbb2-a56dc7ba00d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0541a8e-593e-5a77-bbb2-a56dc7ba00d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463529} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0761348-b2bc-5d51-a4a4-3ecdf8745d6a" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bb28647b-13b7-5f23-9064-5edced19689d" :question/math-academy-id "q-125668" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6ed50407066da9fc213202ccff8c8be06c89d2dce0f5dfe07877cab77c98b3ec.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ are false. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves around $C,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/04/045f6867a50dff0c162376015cc4651de796d0a637643b4b5ba402ef55dde4fa.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ remains unchanged.\n\n![](images/69/698f68b9539e6ef5c4b07dbe6cf3859449e2687db19406f6c2b0072fa5eb697e.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2433c883-9454-5783-a42b-a158449a6704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369293} {:answer/id #uuid "da8f4541-beae-50fa-837a-88c5c1315ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369294} {:answer/id #uuid "94ddba9c-b5d2-5aad-bbd2-1982a2662332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369295} {:answer/id #uuid "759a9631-bed4-55f7-ba67-742c0198c7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369296} {:answer/id #uuid "40433ff5-a4f9-59d7-b1cf-0b7ff6dd7d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40433ff5-a4f9-59d7-b1cf-0b7ff6dd7d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369297} :answer-field/id #uuid "e70cc117-b909-56f1-8961-8a545df9549f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "15f53228-e106-54bd-8baa-01a5e8c54996" :question/math-academy-id "q-125484" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=2x\\,i+2y\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=9$ oriented counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our curve as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThe closed curve $C$ is the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $3$ and $1,$ respectively. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2x\\,i+2y\\,j \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8\\left(\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}\\right)\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-4(-1+1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ccf9fe-9fff-57a9-9304-9ed3ab411a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470949} {:answer/id #uuid "cd38aae3-eb89-502e-95f5-f0b67c9bface" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ccf9fe-9fff-57a9-9304-9ed3ab411a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470949} :answer-field/id #uuid "b676af05-3dc2-57c5-937a-36acc27a6987" :answer-field/key "$F$ is **not** conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471980} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4d25790-233a-5252-8654-1ee93a945a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470951} {:answer/id #uuid "88bef363-90dd-5f58-8f3e-0e6fa9a731c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4d25790-233a-5252-8654-1ee93a945a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470951} :answer-field/id #uuid "b508976c-ce23-5a0b-8ee8-1332aba82f50" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f1634ca-676c-56be-805f-f8a4da6ba9b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470953} {:answer/id #uuid "2d74d261-31ed-592a-8886-2e31a70f20d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f1634ca-676c-56be-805f-f8a4da6ba9b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470953} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a1e2d7d-bec5-5fe7-8248-ae4746a2c58c" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9710463e-4d66-5de0-aa7f-2a13fd536838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669005} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc574f6-f2de-5cb2-80df-71c62786fab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fc574f6-f2de-5cb2-80df-71c62786fab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669006} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a7b498e-8ca9-58dc-9151-1230bcc40ace" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8d4a2162-ef8c-55f6-9a59-3237823f3b0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125660" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=({e}^{x+y}-4x)\\,i+({e}^{x+y}+6y)\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x+y}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$F$ is **not** conservative” is false. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0\n$$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81170187-aa6e-5bfa-b16b-ae1c857eaa1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453312} {:answer/id #uuid "e642b50f-fc15-598c-8734-9ce786c97378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e642b50f-fc15-598c-8734-9ce786c97378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453313} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe6c1faa-915a-575a-9ae6-ee5d18d7b44c" :answer-field/key "$F$ is conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454406} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f5f792-942f-538c-a2b1-487c714d1e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453314} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f7fbd1-2c63-5201-8723-39a46c7046c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2f5f792-942f-538c-a2b1-487c714d1e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453314} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eb914e4-930c-5f8c-ab6a-e6dd516efbdf" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise linear path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454407} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1087b0b5-65bc-5402-a83a-9fd1a34fa46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453316} {:answer/id #uuid "1e0b8f24-fdc6-5b9c-b4c5-c8d4a3661432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e0b8f24-fdc6-5b9c-b4c5-c8d4a3661432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453317} :answer-field/id #uuid "81482706-7dd2-58d4-8c2d-b65933e9d667" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c2e3deb8-e342-5f74-9602-be1fdd94c775" :question/math-academy-id "q-125661" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=({x}^{2}+4y)\\,i+4x\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$F$ is conservative” is true. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any piecewise linear path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false, while statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$F$ is conservative”; “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f9c554b-d6e3-52ed-b916-eff4bbabf9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453318} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2dc769-6e03-5a92-8482-5168690a775a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2dc769-6e03-5a92-8482-5168690a775a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453319} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bdfca1a-584e-538d-a8d3-3072dca98494" :answer-field/key "$F$ is conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454409} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4334bdd4-9c1f-50e7-8b9c-07c6d8fdca99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453320} {:answer/id #uuid "7df7187a-4d59-587f-93cc-9c009e0929d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7df7187a-4d59-587f-93cc-9c009e0929d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453321} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8d8d4b7-46b3-5bcb-ac17-298d14c20437" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454410} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee87d2cb-ee2e-5a8d-a70b-3564d5aa2f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453322} {:answer/id #uuid "fdfdf8ab-48c2-5a0e-a0a2-baf7ed4dcfc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdfdf8ab-48c2-5a0e-a0a2-baf7ed4dcfc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453323} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8edc981-6f69-524a-a43a-a0ba1b3c3778" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "12c57671-3717-5693-b7e2-6cfc6da6f16d" :question/math-academy-id "q-125662" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=(x{e}^{y}+5)\\,i+\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{y}}{2}\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=x{e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$F$ is conservative” is true. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$” and “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” are true. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$F$ is conservative”; “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$”; “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55d9a389-0207-5627-8724-2ab06942a52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472532} {:answer/id #uuid "8021b753-e25f-51ff-8c8f-fab09d9d89b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8021b753-e25f-51ff-8c8f-fab09d9d89b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472533} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f990914-9c06-5321-9dbf-d829370622d6" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f7147a8-f34e-5218-b7c5-8ea2c830c0bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472534} {:answer/id #uuid "308c82b6-5505-533c-a6a4-f3335f961206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308c82b6-5505-533c-a6a4-f3335f961206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472535} :answer-field/id #uuid "be5dec92-40f9-56cc-a873-06f88cbc4087" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "975f0d9b-1723-5cdd-bb95-28c94959e5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472536} {:answer/id #uuid "8caa6e88-f7bc-5579-83d6-8f86c7a5803f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975f0d9b-1723-5cdd-bb95-28c94959e5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472536} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b8664d6-4e9d-52a7-ac0d-f153ff8d27fa" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2e8f010b-1d85-5f55-981d-5803f1cc03c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125645" :question/problem "![](images/98/981d966645eec322afbfe28a5a1f519eeab8b3557692dcce368a87fe748dddd6.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is true, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/b2/b2473eb0c505d75d2c448c1a0d714d05d42737ce8d601401e925834a25ae9e14.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/85/8513d9d15d204b6f63f310a37465d6b8dfb21239ca412bac7d3b9936f2bf5ebf.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0;\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b3484a3-4e24-56fb-b7a3-9ddea884c66d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415285} {:answer/id #uuid "5f428d96-a179-52b0-a209-2ee6f08dffb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415291} {:answer/id #uuid "d9418009-409d-5c05-bc92-ce23127789ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415299} {:answer/id #uuid "e65b56f6-b686-5dc3-9782-652e4c386b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415302} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8f2775-c0fe-5dbb-b5a2-d9f8ae009d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb8f2775-c0fe-5dbb-b5a2-d9f8ae009d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415304} :answer-field/id #uuid "8daab46c-8511-5579-956f-63a995a70f85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4ec2acb3-1493-5600-bce3-9a9694ba6ec0" :question/math-academy-id "q-125470" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=y\\,i-x\\,j$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ oriented counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "The closed curve $C$ is the circle of radius $2$ centered at the origin. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i-x\\,j \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-4{sin}^{2}⁡t-4{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-4(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-8\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415314 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51baee7c-4f09-5886-aa36-1dcdf90f0b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472538} {:answer/id #uuid "46738186-25bf-5244-a8cd-2cfae05fe1b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51baee7c-4f09-5886-aa36-1dcdf90f0b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472538} :answer-field/id #uuid "2343f5a2-9a6f-5456-bd97-3e506bdd18a6" :answer-field/key "$F$ is **not** conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d8099c-d11a-55ed-bd66-5bc9bfad9a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472540} {:answer/id #uuid "91e139e0-9b3e-56d8-b8c4-b1714fe1291e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d8099c-d11a-55ed-bd66-5bc9bfad9a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472540} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7751525-7c16-596e-8c69-5d8f650009fe" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "860e69b6-35d8-5d31-ba12-9202b482813d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472542} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8bf411-3432-5e8d-81ec-008c129f27d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8bf411-3432-5e8d-81ec-008c129f27d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472543} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f14689-536e-5986-8e63-f7f4a981a39f" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d95761ef-ef8a-59a8-8e89-af33add923ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669003} {:answer/id #uuid "e7735880-3d1a-574a-b1d0-0f7e2aa996db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d95761ef-ef8a-59a8-8e89-af33add923ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669003} :answer-field/id #uuid "75dc52ae-6fcb-587b-862d-316f1cbc03a3" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "77e87c43-f6db-5082-9277-93ef32960dff" :question/math-academy-id "q-125659" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡2y\\,i+\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{1+4{y}^{2}}\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4x}{1+4{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$F$ is **not** conservative” is false. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false, while statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f4c3d7-9a04-5668-b2e0-7bc01b46d0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415282} {:answer/id #uuid "50325077-b1b2-55cc-a916-71cd3fe9281a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415288} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f96501-879d-531b-beaa-b191c153f318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415297} {:answer/id #uuid "afd3784e-7e64-5098-b432-0a060374a546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415298} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb55bf7-4c03-598b-b1a4-e6045754359b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50325077-b1b2-55cc-a916-71cd3fe9281a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415288} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e78bf84-51cb-53d9-8508-33548a10f308" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b79e3fb3-3865-5932-ba2e-8b5992286bc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-125481" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=-y\\,i+x\\,j$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5$ oriented counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "The closed curve $C$ is the circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ centered at the origin. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =-y\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =5{sin}^{2}⁡t+5{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }5\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =5(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =10\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b7d45a6-b7b5-5b6e-a82c-a1748d83e603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454946} {:answer/id #uuid "7e4f36c3-2d0c-50c9-a36d-272fd914e84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455133} {:answer/id #uuid "c26f1bdf-26e0-5acd-bbc9-1a8e6be78f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455239} {:answer/id #uuid "c3275529-012a-5a31-82a4-2f28fcd1acb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455240} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6f64d6-184a-5394-8a28-a8c004572db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3275529-012a-5a31-82a4-2f28fcd1acb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455240} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbf611c1-7a64-56ff-a8ce-599f171848cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "442b3fed-648b-5cc8-977b-6700ae26738b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125482" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9$ oriented counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "The closed curve $C$ is the circle of radius $3$ centered at the origin. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-1+1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455463 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f5e806-242d-5b1a-8886-66c2da17be28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454981} {:answer/id #uuid "5b31d58a-98fe-5653-8b2e-f0931877d07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455066} {:answer/id #uuid "708e66ed-fb9c-572e-9876-d3e2f4e3957c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455113} {:answer/id #uuid "814fc88c-5be7-5618-be65-2f99b06af468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455137} {:answer/id #uuid "e34fc7a8-8d96-5fc5-a347-b84cc10b6757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b31d58a-98fe-5653-8b2e-f0931877d07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455066} :answer-field/id #uuid "82c6016b-0343-53a1-a3ae-36d3278711ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "674f4764-9a63-51ae-b803-b7fdf438bb38" :question/math-academy-id "q-125667" :question/problem "![](images/13/13e4c6a06a44099024ce91ef6c9ed4679af037c2e794351597a4d604bf39dc6f.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves around $C,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/63/6371bb04d33719ee18c65a92354e84be0e9077e780eac9559dcb7ec42deb8d99.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ remains unchanged.\n\n![](images/0b/0bd9476fa9b19f04b40fbb9cca2986ed90495aa134307606622ef91070af19a7.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029ef420-9eaa-5c6d-8287-3ef33710e976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454907} {:answer/id #uuid "3af01276-3947-5c77-abb0-001b7f9268cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455000} {:answer/id #uuid "74a31f1c-47e3-545d-a815-1b80644ceb5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455118} {:answer/id #uuid "c134f711-db33-5b9e-bc96-94b44710886e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455236} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1d9b86-ba57-557d-9af4-ca1029204f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af01276-3947-5c77-abb0-001b7f9268cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455000} :answer-field/id #uuid "07b21c95-dc62-58a4-b763-c93eafdfda09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a9318e5b-e833-584c-92bb-558dab7e94de" :question/math-academy-id "q-125640" :question/problem "![](images/a1/a1883ee3a3a99d43109bae2d2093aef35548dde9753cfb7dc19dfd77a104ec83.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/85/8595904122fac3431fc959b2fa4aa5a3062bd1bffd1a391a0861fa12f2498054.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $C.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1f31f2b6eefddedc46b8e845703904c0b4566963e64a644f7a4ab32bb7240c3.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455487 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40242699-9a76-5769-ad29-253e8f600b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455010} {:answer/id #uuid "63642342-0ea8-5389-ae31-2bce908c8ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455082} {:answer/id #uuid "90199dc9-7e02-5cd1-bdd7-df4867251c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455163} {:answer/id #uuid "97eeaf90-7d49-5a72-b321-ee76bbb6e4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455176} {:answer/id #uuid "c097de0b-9eac-5b4e-97f4-50838319facf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97eeaf90-7d49-5a72-b321-ee76bbb6e4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455176} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2afbdbe-c2b8-5f8b-8cd1-c52860a3b3d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "afd2a4b0-18e7-5bc4-9563-64bdaef16530" :question/math-academy-id "q-125666" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d042734a8c7483c54795cd6ec8527b43f398cb77487d054a36b27d704f27a318.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/f8/f8268167bb50f9d03cb38a3d505fa6b40003e307b149356089f5b0dc3dd32110.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/a8/a83934aa58040b4eb2bb957d1d12caba676e306e41086480d064935eab9f1c59.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455499 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7781bfa2-360a-52f2-b8a7-5fd12172c6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455124} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad5e1c3-fe87-52c4-9343-a5e560de27a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455128} {:answer/id #uuid "9a55b0b7-ffd1-54c4-8119-7e1a1a488949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455185} {:answer/id #uuid "b6715a23-2351-5f62-8ba5-ef943e459d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455223} {:answer/id #uuid "c19b819d-c541-51b6-a6e0-7dae5f0106b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6715a23-2351-5f62-8ba5-ef943e459d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455223} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd93af99-5bab-55c2-8a85-e0d5efec7517" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d78a254d-adb2-5551-a797-0a608524ca4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-125669" :question/problem "![](images/36/36ebce64036b7661c81aa6525c407f698375544532985175cc465ddc3ff4f5a8.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement III is false. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves around $C,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/c4/c498ddeae8ba4325a4a1dfc0840520c4718bb50a0600970405374dde933e1b1d.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ remains unchanged.\n\n![](images/74/740429a29b5eb4b72bbfae11e08c9ac272e72e31d395b4dad2602beb4d4ba40a.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "083c5ede-cedd-556a-8b65-fe48a6829892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500481} {:answer/id #uuid "119acc6e-65cb-58c0-bc0c-21f9dc698553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500505} {:answer/id #uuid "96e02c89-8c88-58ca-a757-3724f4c8eaae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500775} {:answer/id #uuid "bfcca706-e138-501f-b9cf-da409da5c70b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500865} {:answer/id #uuid "d6603e3d-1da4-5eb2-b8fd-71573abd6fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96e02c89-8c88-58ca-a757-3724f4c8eaae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500775} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb54f63-1362-5d2e-8c6a-5e8e2485a25f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5f7aceb3-5a6a-584b-8488-47f8fb82e9a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-125649" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f178c33254644c5e2e7bf6f3c596df87b1ea2f0b5bfd417c3f279f6c62b1b0d.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/f8/f87d2e735ad58e0b33a813fb91ab202ac0eeaf90575979ea45f954fb7e1d0493.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/10/102c11f9002e29a3759679c6ff0bd10188908d33eb9cc94a84d900956adc33a5.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2060f8ff-9db5-5ae3-9b8b-714361a5c1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708867} {:answer/id #uuid "6f72bab8-faa5-5f8c-9e8a-8ceafadc74d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708873} {:answer/id #uuid "70644d1d-55cd-5ae2-a7b1-cceeff55bffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708875} {:answer/id #uuid "99e15655-6846-5b85-b864-a84d6ac10e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708877} {:answer/id #uuid "aaea2090-b42f-5326-911a-6882ea7300a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2060f8ff-9db5-5ae3-9b8b-714361a5c1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708867} :answer-field/id #uuid "a452b6d3-c627-5b39-80c1-6ab82a525566" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "31ae981b-4492-5f23-bfff-db7fb6aa17bc" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf i-x\\,\\mathbf j$ along the closed curve $C$ traversed once according to\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=3\\cos t\\,\\mathbf i+2\\sin t\\,\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation is the work done by $\\mathbf F$ around the entire closed curve:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong $C$, we have $x=3\\cos t$ and $y=2\\sin t$. Substituting these coordinates into the field and differentiating the path gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=2\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i-3\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=-3\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+2\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product, keeping the signs of both components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=(2\\sin t)(-3\\sin t)+(-3\\cos t)(2\\cos t)\\\\\n&=-6\\sin^2t-6\\cos^2t=-6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\int_0^{2\\pi}-6\\,\\mathrm dt\n=\\left[-6t\\right]_0^{2\\pi}=-12\\pi.\n$$\n\nThe parametrization moves counterclockwise, while the field opposes that motion, consistent with the negative result."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708869 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa025255-d585-50ff-8238-793b46e9dc29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa025255-d585-50ff-8238-793b46e9dc29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708882} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fbe158b-9d3d-5a9a-84bd-29efb5f420c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "34bf737e-a3ae-5c48-928a-57190e62bc89" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(x-y)\\,\\mathbf i+(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the ellipse $x^2+4y^2=4$, traversed once clockwise. Give an exact answer.\n\n$\\Gamma=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The ellipse has equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{2^2}+\\frac{y^2}{1^2}=1.\n$$\n\nTo traverse it clockwise, use\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=2\\cos t\\,\\mathbf i-\\sin t\\,\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $(2,0)$ the velocity is $(0,-1)$, so this parametrization starts downward and has the required orientation. Along the path, $x=2\\cos t$ and $y=-\\sin t$. Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=(2\\cos t+\\sin t)\\,\\mathbf i+(2\\cos t-\\sin t)\\,\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=-2\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i-\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe dot product contains a term that varies along the ellipse:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=-2\\sin t(2\\cos t+\\sin t)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\cos t(2\\cos t-\\sin t)\\\\\n&=-4\\sin t\\cos t-2\\sin^2t\\\\\n&\\quad-2\\cos^2t+\\sin t\\cos t\\\\\n&=-2-3\\sin t\\cos t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate over one complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\\n&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}(-2-3\\sin t\\cos t)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[-2t-\\frac32\\sin^2t\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=-4\\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe varying term integrates to zero over the closed path; it cannot simply be discarded pointwise. The negative sign agrees with clockwise traversal against the rotational part of the field."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708871 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05dbf953-3e15-5944-b83d-8111664ce313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708866} {:answer/id #uuid "5bbcf6ba-466a-5981-bc2b-5cd284620704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708872} {:answer/id #uuid "76946aca-f5c7-5733-915b-7f600db1449e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708876} {:answer/id #uuid "c0febd35-10e2-53c9-887f-e1bebdf1037e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708880} {:answer/id #uuid "eb0318ea-f438-5732-88d6-85685e8b0145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bbcf6ba-466a-5981-bc2b-5cd284620704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708872} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b398cfe-1e3c-5651-9539-d68e8ce36cd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "406aa000-029e-55fb-b2fa-2c84e114b605" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf i+x\\,\\mathbf j$ along the ellipse\n\n$$\n4x^2+y^2=16,\n$$\n\ntraversed once counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "Write the ellipse in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{2^2}+\\frac{y^2}{4^2}=1.\n$$\n\nIts horizontal and vertical semiaxes are $2$ and $4$. A parametrization that traces it once counterclockwise is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=2\\cos t\\,\\mathbf i+4\\sin t\\,\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$ the path starts at $(2,0)$ and moves upward, confirming the orientation. The circulation is\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the ellipse, $x=2\\cos t$ and $y=4\\sin t$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=-4\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+2\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=-2\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+4\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTaking the dot product gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=(-4\\sin t)(-2\\sin t)+(2\\cos t)(4\\cos t)\\\\\n&=8\\sin^2t+8\\cos^2t=8.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\int_0^{2\\pi}8\\,\\mathrm dt\n=\\left[8t\\right]_0^{2\\pi}=16\\pi.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "687b9f6f-e7f6-589f-86d2-1c035a977037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708922} {:answer/id #uuid "f743fc4a-6ce2-5dd5-b734-8f94962784fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "687b9f6f-e7f6-589f-86d2-1c035a977037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708922} :answer-field/id #uuid "161d9dc7-29f1-5b7a-9e51-f3e47f54ab43" :answer-field/key "$W_\\alpha+W_\\beta-W_\\gamma=0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78725412-f445-52e3-ba0c-db8001bf49ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708924} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c294ca-1374-50cb-b5c0-c369ba91fb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78725412-f445-52e3-ba0c-db8001bf49ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708924} :answer-field/id #uuid "45a1ea62-0736-5818-a52f-7fc39a291dd3" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_L\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every piecewise-smooth closed path $L$ in $\\mathbb R^2$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708915} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "127f8b00-dfe8-5662-9213-6be17d5f677c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708904} {:answer/id #uuid "709a61f1-a360-59c3-9cf3-3c7df997751c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "127f8b00-dfe8-5662-9213-6be17d5f677c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708904} :answer-field/id #uuid "79bb9d74-d97f-53d5-9e12-3245a2507a0e" :answer-field/key "$W_\\alpha+W_\\beta+W_\\gamma=0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708925} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a753cfd-0a7c-5fff-938e-4cbe3b392cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708913} {:answer/id #uuid "ed25e50e-6a13-5096-9927-a1ffa0a36e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a753cfd-0a7c-5fff-938e-4cbe3b392cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708913} :answer-field/id #uuid "e49722d5-e084-5b8b-9ec4-07645f516aea" :answer-field/key "$W_\\gamma=0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "64a3e978-5531-584f-b773-52ddb4bbf1c1" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(y+1)\\,\\mathbf i+(x+2y)\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. The diagram shows three piecewise-smooth directed paths: $\\alpha$ goes from $A$ to $B$, $\\beta$ from $B$ to $C$, and $\\gamma$ from $A$ to $C$.\n\n![Directed paths alpha from A to B, beta from B to C, and gamma from A to C.](images/6e/6e8f8843f36ab175203206494f36a05c0c24fc4998a6c3fb0e4e0556ccc1e959.png)\n\nFor any directed path $\\eta$, write $W_\\eta=\\int_\\eta\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$. You are given $W_\\alpha=1$ and $W_\\beta=2$.\n\nWhich statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First establish that the field is conservative. With $P=y+1$ and $Q=x+2y$,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=1=\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}.\n$$\n\nBoth components have continuous partial derivatives on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb R^2$. Thus $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, and every closed-path circulation is zero.\n\nFollowing $\\alpha$, then $\\beta$, then the reverse of $\\gamma$ returns to $A$. Reversing a path changes the sign of its work. Therefore,\n\n$$\nW_\\alpha+W_\\beta-W_\\gamma=0,\n\\qquad W_\\gamma=1+2=3.\n$$\n\nEquivalently, the route through $B$ and the direct route have the same endpoints, so path independence gives the same work along them.\n\n- The equation $W_\\alpha+W_\\beta-W_\\gamma=0$ is true: it expresses the circulation around that closed route.\n- The equation $W_\\gamma=0$ is false: $W_\\gamma=3$, not zero. The path $\\gamma$ is open.\n- The equation $W_\\alpha+W_\\beta+W_\\gamma=0$ is false: $W_\\alpha+W_\\beta+W_\\gamma=1+2+3=6$. The plus sign on $W_\\gamma$ does not represent the return path.\n- The zero-circulation statement is true for every piecewise-smooth closed path, regardless of its shape or orientation.\n\nSelect $W_\\alpha+W_\\beta-W_\\gamma=0$ and the statement that every closed path has zero circulation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51816e2b-ad05-50de-a947-895da8989fc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708918} {:answer/id #uuid "a839a4c9-feb3-55a3-83ad-ea8b41a70aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51816e2b-ad05-50de-a947-895da8989fc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708918} :answer-field/id #uuid "355bb441-24c8-567e-9be7-c18f9a0a06c7" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every ellipse $C$, in either orientation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708910} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "388bbfe7-8efc-5f73-a008-b9bb950f8eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708912} {:answer/id #uuid "ab38777c-1f74-5630-8fd5-28dec17326d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "388bbfe7-8efc-5f73-a008-b9bb950f8eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708912} :answer-field/id #uuid "3de8582f-59e6-560e-88de-60cd0c12ac63" :answer-field/key "$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every path $C$, including open paths." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13f6f214-16fb-51d1-aec7-032ac9ed9548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708905} {:answer/id #uuid "2dc2c7a3-7e7e-5482-9943-3a407819756d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dc2c7a3-7e7e-5482-9943-3a407819756d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708909} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b222b31-8b84-5c77-84bb-c87a22458b17" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is not conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "98818319-f2d6-505a-ba3c-1576aa4128a7" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(y^2+x)\\,\\mathbf i+(2xy+1)\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. Which statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. All paths below are piecewise smooth and lie in $\\mathbb R^2$." :question/worked-solution "Write $P=y^2+x$ and $Q=2xy+1$. Their cross partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=2y=\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}.\n$$\n\nThe components have continuous partial derivatives everywhere on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb R^2$, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative.\n\n- The claim that $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative is false: $\\mathbf F$ is conservative.\n- The claim that every path has zero work is false. For example, on the line segment from $(0,0)$ to $(1,0)$, we have $y=0$ and $\\mathrm dy=0$, so the work is $\\int_0^1 x\\,\\mathrm dx=\\tfrac12$, not zero.\n- The claim about ellipses is true. Every ellipse is a closed curve, and the circulation of a conservative field around any closed curve is zero. Reversing the orientation still gives zero.\n\nSelect only the statement that every ellipse has zero circulation in either orientation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4df31c52-bc01-5b25-90c7-2e8375ccc0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708917} {:answer/id #uuid "9c07fc97-8425-51f5-87e5-7063e4630369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4df31c52-bc01-5b25-90c7-2e8375ccc0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708917} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c10103b-3b87-554d-bb4a-4f4e7d30bbb5" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47bb2438-1e1e-5f08-9387-7c00bf570132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708916} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae8e507-b0ac-5285-8f70-5906a81a2686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ae8e507-b0ac-5285-8f70-5906a81a2686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708919} :answer-field/id #uuid "37a25ca8-d07e-5fd6-a30c-dfc2efe2d44b" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every closed path $C$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "144dc0cf-eb7b-50b8-a537-f7785de55a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708906} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b7748c-c2ca-554d-9088-ae1553054763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "144dc0cf-eb7b-50b8-a537-f7785de55a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708906} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee383afc-ba12-50a7-851f-82f188936eba" :answer-field/key "$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every path $C$, including open paths." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ce67a928-0f09-56e4-b75d-c6598ccee7fe" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=x^2+y^2$ on $\\mathbb R^2$ and let $\\mathbf F=\\nabla f$. Which statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. All paths below are piecewise smooth and lie in $\\mathbb R^2$." :question/worked-solution "The field $\\mathbf F=\\nabla f$ is conservative by definition. The fundamental theorem of line integrals gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=f(B)-f(A),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are the starting and ending points.\n\n- The claim that every path has zero work is false. An open path need not have zero work: from $(0,0)$ to $(1,0)$, the work is $1-0=1$.\n- The claim that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative is true because $f$ is a potential function for $\\mathbf F$.\n- The claim that every closed path has zero circulation is true. A closed path has the same starting and ending point, so its circulation is $f(A)-f(A)=0$, in either orientation.\n\nSelect “$\\mathbf F$ is conservative” and the statement that every closed path has zero circulation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4595e8f9-8da6-5282-82de-e879496c8f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709122} {:answer/id #uuid "7580e5c3-bc36-529b-93db-ed5ac1584ea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709134} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf1a9ec-4e0b-5d8f-a473-fb939ec13e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709146} {:answer/id #uuid "ebba7eea-be14-5be9-8c53-7b7e2c4b767a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709156} {:answer/id #uuid "fd81e417-18b1-5cf7-bb7b-97a19a1586ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebba7eea-be14-5be9-8c53-7b7e2c4b767a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709156} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0be711e-ec85-5ff5-8dfc-b96685885b96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "17b8a05f-19be-5afe-8433-84207e8b21e1" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a418ee1077c0ff02e482de48f0bd2b6ea9d9349afd2383982268e671d721d4ac.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse and vector field $\\mathbf F$ shown above. Let $C$ traverse the curve once in the **counterclockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$\n\nII. $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$\n\nIII. $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r = 0$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ measures the work done around a *closed* curve. Assistance gives positive work, opposition gives negative work, and perpendicular force gives zero work.\n\nThe field opposes the motion all the way around $C$ in the **counterclockwise** direction.\n\n![](images/ff/ff9321c7e89f068bdea219704e49308395c70d38ed5632d4825dd53d891aa7f7.png)\n\nThus, $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$. Reversing traversal reverses the work: $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$. The reversed path $-C$ is **clockwise**.\n\n![](images/e3/e39aa75ea70dbcbac17d4a5c3a1e2a36e5f3675878c514ee3591d2ce8f127d8f.png)\n\nTherefore, $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$.\n\nI. $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$ is **false**.\n\nII. $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$ is **true**.\n\nIII. $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r = 0$ is **false**.\n\nThe true statements are II only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ab90bd-ac6f-52bf-b52d-7cc6c97d04a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709119} {:answer/id #uuid "55be1f06-1043-5517-ad27-23ebf39f8def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :a