\n\nConsider the ellipse and vector field $\\mathbf F$ shown above. Let $C$ traverse the curve once in the **counterclockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ measures the work done around a *closed* curve. Assistance gives positive work, opposition gives negative work, and perpendicular force gives zero work.\n\nThe field assists the motion all the way around $C$ in the **counterclockwise** direction.\n\n![](images/8e/8e1e410cfb38556ebefa6d344f954e3256052a35cf3ad05a4270fe3d34806024.png)\n\nThus, $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$. Reversing traversal reverses the work: $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$. The reversed path $-C$ is **clockwise**.\n\n![](images/15/1590415f4323f7b56283f9718f04a433c235a5e6461eb8239f3dc745f7651923.png)\n\nTherefore, $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$.\n\n- $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$ is **true**.\n\n- $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$ is **false**.\n\n- $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$ is **false**.\n\nTherefore, select $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bec6263-241c-596e-93b6-32079a604faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709159} {:answer/id #uuid "2e44967a-2637-5c16-aa79-aff4590fe535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709160} {:answer/id #uuid "4d75b248-eb10-5fb0-b38b-7246c7e778f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709161} {:answer/id #uuid "8aea9b5b-f64c-5f5b-945d-c29beba8d51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709163} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d45f19-e562-5cdf-989e-c926ed031c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d75b248-eb10-5fb0-b38b-7246c7e778f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709161} :answer-field/id #uuid "870a078a-c0e8-53b2-9b2e-279ede96820e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "97ec6f57-5069-56ca-be0f-2c1b13bbed76" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a418ee1077c0ff02e482de48f0bd2b6ea9d9349afd2383982268e671d721d4ac.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse and vector field $\\mathbf F$ shown above. Let $C$ traverse the curve once in the **counterclockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$\n\nII. $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$\n\nIII. $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ measures the work done around a *closed* curve. Assistance gives positive work, opposition gives negative work, and perpendicular force gives zero work.\n\nThe field opposes the motion all the way around $C$ in the **counterclockwise** direction.\n\n![](images/ff/ff9321c7e89f068bdea219704e49308395c70d38ed5632d4825dd53d891aa7f7.png)\n\nThus, $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$. Reversing traversal reverses the work: $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$. The reversed path $-C$ is **clockwise**.\n\n![](images/e3/e39aa75ea70dbcbac17d4a5c3a1e2a36e5f3675878c514ee3591d2ce8f127d8f.png)\n\nTherefore, $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$.\n\nI. $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$ is **true**.\n\nII. $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$ is **true**.\n\nIII. $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$ is **false**.\n\nThe true statements are I and II only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a88e5a4d-8e5b-54db-b625-d11a8f31bebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709170} {:answer/id #uuid "c96960d6-4fb4-5875-9f57-3d82a0c8058b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c96960d6-4fb4-5875-9f57-3d82a0c8058b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709173} :answer-field/id #uuid "0364349e-2713-537e-9312-de149a7b7e16" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2377061-1a27-5fcf-929a-dcc75b9d3609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709171} {:answer/id #uuid "c99111d6-cc35-5095-b340-e424bd863347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2377061-1a27-5fcf-929a-dcc75b9d3609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709171} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e62de53-ec7c-54fb-bf08-61dbf7f9744b" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "218c85d9-2656-5ce1-909f-8f49bffeeeda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709167} {:answer/id #uuid "494ae11c-ef0c-5934-a733-b92fa0cec6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "218c85d9-2656-5ce1-909f-8f49bffeeeda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709167} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7996383-a83b-5637-ae80-161fef669200" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d3d12363-c71b-530e-aa37-25418cc90cb9" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d232b32fc243beced89ed9ebce168352fe42e008d162c6d55bfbacaac829a2e6.png)\n\nConsider the circle and vector field $\\mathbf F$ shown above. Let $C$ traverse the curve once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ measures the work done around a *closed* curve. Assistance gives positive work, opposition gives negative work, and perpendicular force gives zero work.\n\nThe field assists the motion all the way around $C$ in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n![](images/2b/2bc25d16cc39cfe026239e2872a28636580cf71194a77d75d31714f63400fa59.png)\n\nThus, $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$. Reversing traversal reverses the work: $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$. The reversed path $-C$ is **counterclockwise**.\n\n![](images/6e/6efae7bba15ad82db3b87f77c7dcc17d67fa3e37bf41b2a365db87f10852c3df.png)\n\nTherefore, $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$.\n\n- $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$ is **false**.\n\n- $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$ is **true**.\n\n- $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$ is **true**.\n\nTherefore, select $\\oint_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r < 0$ and $\\oint_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r > 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b3b9a9b-5eff-5241-8777-da131a0eb556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709197} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b87499-82ac-51e3-a3d6-106325f32912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709204} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c8b182-54a3-5da4-9677-32abe43904e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709205} {:answer/id #uuid "be2a5d76-d90b-5bb0-9509-d70b79d3083b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 40 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709206} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c8e489-da31-54c6-8227-30884bb054c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3c8b182-54a3-5da4-9677-32abe43904e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709205} :answer-field/id #uuid "269c00e9-97a2-51b1-bad4-78156a47b7b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "024cc830-6486-5ab7-a5ef-c743de344510" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(y\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- x\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the ellipse $C$ with equation\n\n$$\n16 x^{2} + 25 y^{2}=400\n$$\n\ntraversed once clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Write the curve in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{16}=1.\n$$\n\nChoose the clockwise parametrization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left(5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$, the path starts at $(5,0)$ and moves downward, confirming the orientation.\n\nCirculation is total work around the closed path:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=20 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad+20 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=20.\n$$\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(20\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[20 t\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=40 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe dot product is constant on this path."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "508aea4d-bec0-5b6b-b75e-c4c5ab99d20f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\sqrt{3} \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709192} {:answer/id #uuid "64da2daf-ddfd-50aa-a392-d729a5edc317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40 \\sqrt{3} \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709195} {:answer/id #uuid "877ab36a-3646-55e0-8b50-d588484736d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 20 \\sqrt{3} \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709198} {:answer/id #uuid "c1812996-ffce-5345-8754-8a25ddf4c3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 40 \\sqrt{3} \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709208} {:answer/id #uuid "d516d27d-f778-5a4c-9c56-245f2e37e997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "877ab36a-3646-55e0-8b50-d588484736d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 20 \\sqrt{3} \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709198} :answer-field/id #uuid "12b0827a-de61-547c-92f0-abcce84e4ea8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "16c8e37b-3767-5c20-8d26-f276ee4dd378" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- 2 y\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(2 x\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the ellipse $C$ with equation\n\n$$\n3 x^{2} + 25 y^{2}=75\n$$\n\ntraversed once clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Write the curve in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nChoose the clockwise parametrization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left(5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$, the path starts at $(5,0)$ and moves downward, confirming the orientation.\n\nCirculation is total work around the closed path:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(2 \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(10 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- \\sqrt{3} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(2 \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(10 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- \\sqrt{3} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 10 \\sqrt{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad-10 \\sqrt{3} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=- 10 \\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(- 10 \\sqrt{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[- 10 \\sqrt{3} t\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=- 20 \\sqrt{3} \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe dot product is constant on this path."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fbb9209-674c-53f8-a36b-152d0cecc054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709202} {:answer/id #uuid "9753e2ef-f977-59bd-8204-44d1769da878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709203} {:answer/id #uuid "bee84380-15af-53bf-b153-8aeaa6bb74fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709207} {:answer/id #uuid "dddae0a7-6388-5939-9411-95014ea5e703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709215} {:answer/id #uuid "e23bd52a-093a-55c0-914a-14fc4b23147a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9753e2ef-f977-59bd-8204-44d1769da878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709203} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef3c55c-a984-5af1-b383-a53299932101" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "47f6bf3b-aa84-523a-a6fd-549467cd649e" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(2 x\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(2 y\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the ellipse $C$ with equation\n\n$$\n25 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}=75\n$$\n\ntraversed once clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Write the curve in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{3}+\\frac{y^2}{25}=1.\n$$\n\nChoose the clockwise parametrization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left(\\sqrt{3} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$, the path starts at $(\\sqrt{3},0)$ and moves downward, confirming the orientation.\n\nCirculation is total work around the closed path:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(2 \\sqrt{3} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(2 \\sqrt{3} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=44 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=44 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\sin^2t=2\\sin t\\cos t$, an antiderivative of $\\sin t\\cos t$ is $\\frac12\\sin^2t$.\n\n\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(44 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[22 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sine-squared term is zero at both endpoints. The varying term therefore integrates to zero; it is not zero at every point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4435c23e-817c-502e-b20f-507d08cbb7a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 100 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709189} {:answer/id #uuid "48a1ffb8-8402-5f25-8cda-5019519a751e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709191} {:answer/id #uuid "56a9a874-2226-51bb-9555-1d7b5eed017c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 25 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709193} {:answer/id #uuid "891483d5-64ad-56f4-9e85-8f2fcaa3bf2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 50 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709199} {:answer/id #uuid "d753eb0d-790b-5593-8030-a83a36dc074a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "891483d5-64ad-56f4-9e85-8f2fcaa3bf2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 50 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709199} :answer-field/id #uuid "d970dc59-ece9-5821-8070-043a5abf0bdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66d5155f-782b-5374-b04f-b8e277295e18" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(y\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- x\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the circle $C$ with equation\n\n$$\nx^{2} + y^{2}=25\n$$\n\ntraversed once counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "Write the curve in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{25}=1.\n$$\n\nChoose the counterclockwise parametrization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left(5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$, the path starts at $(5,0)$ and moves upward, confirming the orientation.\n\nCirculation is total work around the closed path:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 25 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad-25 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=-25.\n$$\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(-25\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[- 25 t\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=- 50 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe dot product is constant on this path."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39a85417-cfd5-56a9-a557-5c6771b07f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709188} {:answer/id #uuid "64bffb91-004e-5187-b0c8-0ea4d5