(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(0\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[0\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe dot product is constant on this path."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de2d4cef-fa66-5c7b-8c28-8e9c2450b160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de2d4cef-fa66-5c7b-8c28-8e9c2450b160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709229} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce4a5ed3-aced-5034-96c1-c2cbbccf10c5" :answer-field/key "value" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "64e5beb1-5e7b-5f60-b79d-82e2e1f0bf0d" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- x - 2 y\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(2 x + 2 y\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the circle $C$ with equation\n\n$$\nx^{2} + y^{2}=1\n$$\n\ntraversed once clockwise. Give an exact answer.\n\n$\\Gamma=$ {{value}}" :question/worked-solution "Write the curve in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{1}+\\frac{y^2}{1}=1.\n$$\n\nChoose the clockwise parametrization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$, the path starts at $(1,0)$ and moves downward, confirming the orientation.\n\nCirculation is total work around the closed path:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad-2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad+3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\sin^2t=2\\sin t\\cos t$, an antiderivative of $\\sin t\\cos t$ is $\\frac12\\sin^2t$.\n\n\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[- 2 t + \\frac{3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}}{2}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=- 4 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sine-squared term is zero at both endpoints. The varying term therefore integrates to zero; it is not zero at every point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709224 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17dea7f2-dabf-5ee3-99c8-7eeead57fa02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\sqrt{5} \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17dea7f2-dabf-5ee3-99c8-7eeead57fa02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\sqrt{5} \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709219} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c08e953-9c4d-527b-9ec6-cad0df957244" :answer-field/key "value" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9e5d7d17-b70a-5efb-a26b-5797573a6b36" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- x + 2 y\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- 2 x - y\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the ellipse $C$ with equation\n\n$$\n5 x^{2} + 4 y^{2}=20\n$$\n\ntraversed once counterclockwise. Give an exact answer.\n\n$\\Gamma=$ {{value}}" :question/worked-solution "Write the curve in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{y^2}{5}=1.\n$$\n\nChoose the counterclockwise parametrization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(\\sqrt{5} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$, the path starts at $(2,0)$ and moves upward, confirming the orientation.\n\nCirculation is total work around the closed path:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(2 \\sqrt{5} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- \\sqrt{5} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(\\sqrt{5} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(2 \\sqrt{5} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(- \\sqrt{5} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(\\sqrt{5} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 4 \\sqrt{5} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad-4 \\sqrt{5} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\sin^2t=2\\sin t\\cos t$, an antiderivative of $\\sin t\\cos t$ is $\\frac12\\sin^2t$.\n\n\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\sqrt{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[- 4 \\sqrt{5} t - \\frac{\\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}}{2}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=- 8 \\sqrt{5} \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sine-squared term is zero at both endpoints. The varying term therefore integrates to zero; it is not zero at every point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92f06f1f-d444-5c7f-b95d-e510d78da644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92f06f1f-d444-5c7f-b95d-e510d78da644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709223} :answer-field/id #uuid "23faa981-21ae-545b-9846-8280a4029944" :answer-field/key "value" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bc4970ec-d34d-5a3e-a955-bb4df945a284" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- x - 2 y\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(2 x + y\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the circle $C$ with equation\n\n$$\nx^{2} + y^{2}=4\n$$\n\ntraversed once counterclockwise. Give an exact answer.\n\n$\\Gamma=$ {{value}}" :question/worked-solution "Write the curve in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nChoose the counterclockwise parametrization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$, the path starts at $(2,0)$ and moves upward, confirming the orientation.\n\nCirculation is total work around the closed path:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=8 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad+8 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad+8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 8.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\sin^2t=2\\sin t\\cos t$, an antiderivative of $\\sin t\\cos t$ is $\\frac12\\sin^2t$.\n\n\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 8\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[8 t + 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=16 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sine-squared term is zero at both endpoints. The varying term therefore integrates to zero; it is not zero at every point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd0ac9be-6732-5f10-9939-9829112a55ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd0ac9be-6732-5f10-9939-9829112a55ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709227} :answer-field/id #uuid "efcb1eae-c092-5524-a4ef-44e2f19ba532" :answer-field/key "value" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c59577b0-319b-5f63-9845-5e6aeec4c101" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(y\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nalong the ellipse $C$ with equation\n\n$$\n9 x^{2} + 4 y^{2}=36\n$$\n\ntraversed once counterclockwise. Give an exact answer.\n\n$\\Gamma=$ {{value}}" :question/worked-solution "Write the curve in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{y^2}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nChoose the counterclockwise parametrization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$, the path starts at $(2,0)$ and moves upward, confirming the orientation.\n\nCirculation is total work around the closed path:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma=\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the path into the field and differentiate the path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(- 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\mathbf r\\prime(t)&=\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the dot product of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\\\\n&=\\left(- 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=17 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1$ and collecting terms gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=17 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\sin^2t=2\\sin t\\cos t$, an antiderivative of $\\sin t\\cos t$ is $\\frac12\\sin^2t$.\n\n\n\nIntegrate over the complete traversal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Gamma&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\left(17 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{17 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}}{2}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}\\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sine-squared term is zero at both endpoints. The varying term therefore integrates to zero; it is not zero at every point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3151d9db-f705-5b45-83e3-ed3fbca7917f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709241} {:answer/id #uuid "a952c573-53ed-5734-bc4c-ef70b5737589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a952c573-53ed-5734-bc4c-ef70b5737589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709279} :answer-field/id #uuid "36400bbe-1d06-58c4-824a-577309cfebc9" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every closed path $C$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c92d8b-bbbf-553c-b89a-32394be3e1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709234} {:answer/id #uuid "d38ebf91-adbe-58f8-b8ee-df6d6256f275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d38ebf91-adbe-58f8-b8ee-df6d6256f275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709287} :answer-field/id #uuid "570acb34-7faa-5c31-ac51-9d0d3e7b4f1d" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b838245-17be-5de8-bff9-356c61e5b00a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709263} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f29943-6ceb-5864-ba7c-412b6ea2f2b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0f29943-6ceb-5864-ba7c-412b6ea2f2b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709291} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cf7798-4323-557e-bdae-862925a3bb55" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "093222ab-1c28-5fb0-be9a-427a15e68dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709231} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2e16b0-2a90-577b-bc17-5eefb04b5a2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "093222ab-1c28-5fb0-be9a-427a15e68dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709231} :answer-field/id #uuid "c50578c9-79e1-5453-bfa8-b58026cd961e" :answer-field/key "$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some open path $C$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709283}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66b0434f-c3b7-55eb-b6b1-0dae427483e5" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(x + 3 y^{2}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(6 x y - 1\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply. All paths mentioned are piecewise smooth and lie in $\\mathbb R^2$." :question/worked-solution "Write $P=x + 3 y^{2}$ and $Q=6 x y - 1$. The cross partials are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=6 y\\\\Q_x&=6 y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThey agree everywhere. The components have continuous partial derivatives on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb R^2$, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative. For a conservative field with potential $f$, the fundamental theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=f(B)-f(A).\n$$\n\nFor such a conservative field, a closed path has the same endpoints, so its circulation is zero in either orientation. An open path can also have zero work when its endpoint potential values agree; zero work is not guaranteed for every open path. For example, the work along the segment from $(0, 0)$ to $(1, 0)$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$, which is nonzero. A path followed by its reverse always has zero total work, so a claim of nonzero work for every closed path is false.\n\n- $\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every closed path $C$. This is **true**.\n- $\\mathbf F$ is conservative. This is **true**.\n- $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some open path $C$. This is **true**.\n- None of the above This is **false**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 1759