 :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c76e7fb7-881d-59f6-b031-b0a795010fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709284} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce25c66-dc27-58e6-97f8-ed3955409d84" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $C$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "752a66b7-5a5d-55b1-9d63-33b7734fc716" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(6 x \\arctan{\\left(2 y \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(\\frac{6 x^{2}}{4 y^{2} + 1} - y\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply. All paths mentioned are piecewise smooth and lie in $\\mathbb R^2$." :question/worked-solution "Write $P=6 x \\arctan{\\left(2 y \\right)}$ and $Q=\\frac{6 x^{2}}{4 y^{2} + 1} - y$. The cross partials are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=\\frac{12 x}{4 y^{2} + 1}\\\\Q_x&=\\frac{12 x}{4 y^{2} + 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThey agree everywhere. The components have continuous partial derivatives on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb R^2$, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative. For a conservative field with potential $f$, the fundamental theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=f(B)-f(A).\n$$\n\nFor such a conservative field, a closed path has the same endpoints, so its circulation is zero in either orientation. An open path can also have zero work when its endpoint potential values agree; zero work is not guaranteed for every open path. For example, the work along the segment from $(0, 0)$ to $(0, 1)$ is $- \\frac{1}{2}$, which is nonzero. A path followed by its reverse always has zero total work, so a claim of nonzero work for every closed path is false.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is conservative. This is **true**.\n- $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some open path $C$. This is **true**.\n- $\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $C$. This is **false**.\n- None of the above This is **false**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa677685-08b7-5880-a2e3-1199dcabe0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709280} {:answer/id #uuid "b862438e-3eed-5209-97b3-48de7f48b4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa677685-08b7-5880-a2e3-1199dcabe0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709280} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d4765ab-e921-541f-8c2a-96ebb2134868" :answer-field/key "$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some open path $C$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c93d0cf2-f9de-52e8-b611-04a1265f5cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709285} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ea9fad-02eb-5c09-afdb-423a2fcfafa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c93d0cf2-f9de-52e8-b611-04a1265f5cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709285} :answer-field/id #uuid "43bc899a-a412-5fda-bbd3-153bc9b44584" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for every closed path $C$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c71c0c5-d5a4-523c-8930-8090fc3ab608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709268} {:answer/id #uuid "972e8d41-9e7e-57c2-89e1-db2a23e4b529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c71c0c5-d5a4-523c-8930-8090fc3ab608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709268} :answer-field/id #uuid "51e3ede8-5e25-5559-8eb9-c50b0d014683" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e80a5a0-0105-5813-a560-6d54e38132d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709274} {:answer/id #uuid "a82aa624-5161-5090-9130-079ac580dc4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a82aa624-5161-5090-9130-079ac580dc4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709278} :answer-field/id #uuid "a00d31c8-3adc-582c-b6b0-40544bd1dff6" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "81c18e9a-74d5-5aae-9b49-97c38c45e90d" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{2 x}{x^{2} + y^{2} + 1}\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(\\frac{2 y}{x^{2} + y^{2} + 1}\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply. All paths mentioned are piecewise smooth and lie in $\\mathbb R^2$." :question/worked-solution "Write $P=\\frac{2 x}{x^{2} + y^{2} + 1}$ and $Q=\\frac{2 y}{x^{2} + y^{2} + 1}$. The cross partials are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=- \\frac{4 x y}{\\left(x^{2} + y^{2} + 1\\right)^{2}}\\\\Q_x&=- \\frac{4 x y}{\\left(x^{2} + y^{2} + 1\\right)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThey agree everywhere. The components have continuous partial derivatives on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb R^2$, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative. For a conservative field with potential $f$, the fundamental theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=f(B)-f(A).\n$$\n\nFor such a conservative field, a closed path has the same endpoints, so its circulation is zero in either orientation. An open path can also have zero work when its endpoint potential values agree; zero work is not guaranteed for every open path. For example, the work along the segment from $(0, 0)$ to $(1, 0)$ is $\\log{\\left(2 \\right)}$, which is nonzero. A path followed by its reverse always has zero total work, so a claim of nonzero work for every closed path is false.\n\n- $\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for every closed path $C$. This is **false**.\n- $\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative. This is **false**.\n- $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some open path $C$. This is **true**.\n- None of the above This is **false**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dea7b88-2fc1-51c9-80e4-44eec747f32a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709238} {:answer/id #uuid "84f91036-8ea1-50ff-b043-f067404f8bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84f91036-8ea1-50ff-b043-f067404f8bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709265} :answer-field/id #uuid "167ac177-ba40-50d1-ae58-f7029d36497d" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every closed path $C$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65f53594-7850-5cf0-b3d2-8319384e10e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709253} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9b889d-a42a-5c5e-8c6c-f033ef0b6657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd9b889d-a42a-5c5e-8c6c-f033ef0b6657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709286} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b64a9e8-53d8-5a3d-9a0d-5a7d2686d454" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35934d8d-e650-5532-a90d-618782aee374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709242} {:answer/id #uuid "57c6379c-cfc7-5fed-ad73-135746cdb337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57c6379c-cfc7-5fed-ad73-135746cdb337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709249} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1135373-53e5-57c3-bbd9-5b396f1666d8" :answer-field/key "$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some open path $C$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709289} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40bccb28-ad09-5165-bffb-caad54fb1c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709244} {:answer/id #uuid "5e71fad2-2717-500b-a45b-70811cd65e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40bccb28-ad09-5165-bffb-caad54fb1c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709244} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2137ccd-5783-54ef-a830-b545f91a9635" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fa058a30-d461-5942-96b8-97819225b713" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- x^{2} + 2 y\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(3 x - 1\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply. All paths mentioned are piecewise smooth and lie in $\\mathbb R^2$." :question/worked-solution "Write $P=- x^{2} + 2 y$ and $Q=3 x - 1$. The cross partials are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=2\\\\Q_x&=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThey do not agree identically. Equality of the cross partials is necessary for a smooth field to be conservative, so $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative. On this domain, if all closed-path integrals were zero, path independence would give a potential. Thus some closed path has nonzero circulation. For a conservative field with potential $f$, the fundamental theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=f(B)-f(A).\n$$\n\nFor such a conservative field, a closed path has the same endpoints, so its circulation is zero in either orientation. An open path can also have zero work when its endpoint potential values agree; zero work is not guaranteed for every open path. For example, the work along the segment from $(0, 0)$ to $(1, 0)$ is $- \\frac{1}{3}$, which is nonzero. A path followed by its reverse always has zero total work, so a claim of nonzero work for every closed path is false.\n\n- $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some open path $C$. This is **true**.\n- $\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0$ for every closed path $C$. This is **false**.\n- $\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative. This is **true**.\n- None of the above This is **false**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be5ddf7-d983-54e4-8729-eb684ed5e242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709329} {:answer/id #uuid "8e088074-4629-53a0-8f0b-8edfe9d0b3b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0be5ddf7-d983-54e4-8729-eb684ed5e242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709329} :answer-field/id #uuid "03ec290d-8bb8-5952-9920-eed63fb0fca5" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709327} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a2e21ac-7b1c-5e1e-8ec6-b908e56ef0db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709328} {:answer/id #uuid "51870aa4-895e-5d46-9655-eb442ddd3e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51870aa4-895e-5d46-9655-eb442ddd3e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709348} :answer-field/id #uuid "160e3c7d-9cdf-53d2-9d58-b7dafc32380c" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8730fede-3d20-531e-b9b6-742ea1f31819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709361} {:answer/id #uuid "e4802124-8cee-56d4-b72a-9ce36ad37bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8730fede-3d20-531e-b9b6-742ea1f31819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709361} :answer-field/id #uuid "51c199ae-547c-5ea7-9dea-5c8565baeddb" :answer-field/key "$W_{\\beta}=0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5ae6894-635f-5182-8c5c-b2f67773a7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709375} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a88def-9de6-5e64-adac-b3e65a79a8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5ae6894-635f-5182-8c5c-b2f67773a7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709375} :answer-field/id #uuid "752b7e75-c5e3-5afc-9134-a449549a0066" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_L\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $L$ in $\\mathbb R^2$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e765bd-7b7a-5b69-8730-3943e170a3df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709326} {:answer/id #uuid "166436b6-a9d7-5a90-89eb-181e0814160b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "166436b6-a9d7-5a90-89eb-181e0814160b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709333} :answer-field/id #uuid "af2e7640-9af6-5935-9994-0c4750a8d257" :answer-field/key "$-W_{\\alpha}-W_{\\gamma}+W_{\\beta}=0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9d7f8aa0-95f5-546a-80dd-90c14740e0c0" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- y - 1\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- x + 4 y\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. The diagram shows three piecewise-smooth directed paths: $\\alpha$ goes from $A$ to $B$, $\\gamma$ goes from $C$ to $B$, $\\beta$ goes from $C$ to $A$.\n\n![alpha from A to B; gamma from C to B; beta from C to A](images/a1/a158314bab6964f974612675168ca0ae56cd9cbe57b24d1e692182f5d3b4db50.png)\n\nFor a directed path $\\eta$, write $W_\\eta=\\int_\\eta\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$. You are given $W_{\\alpha}=-1$ and $W_{\\gamma}=-1$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Write $P=- y - 1$ and $Q=- x + 4 y$. The cross partials are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=-1\\\\Q_x&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThey agree everywhere. The components have continuous partial derivatives on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb R^2$, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative. For a conservative field with potential $f$, the fundamental theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=f(B)-f(A).\n$$\n\nFor such a conservative field, a closed path has the same endpoints, so its circulation is zero in either orientation. An open path can also have zero work when its endpoint potential values agree; zero work is not guaranteed for every open path. Follow the route $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$. Relative to the displayed arrows, its edge signs give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W_{\\alpha}-W_{\\gamma}+W_{\\beta}&=0\\\\W_{\\beta}&=0\\\\W_{\\beta}&=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReversing an edge changes its work sign. The proposed cycle sum evaluates to $2$. Compare the proposed missing work with $0$.\n\n- $W_{\\beta}=0$. This is **true**.\n- $\\oint_L\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $L$ in $\\mathbb R^2$. This is **false**.\n- $\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative. This is **false**.\n- $-W_{\\alpha}-W_{\\gamma}+W_{\\beta}=0$. This is **false**.\n- None of the above This is **false**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70613de7-d1d5-52d9-b3db-2b9ec697ae29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709355} {:answer/id #uuid "757c512c-492a-51a4-90a5-8259656f7b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70613de7-d1d5-52d9-b3db-2b9ec697ae29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709355} :answer-field/id #uuid "67fe19e3-24e2-52b5-bad6-4a959b37dfad" :answer-field/key "$W_{\\gamma}=0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6944f629-1730-5707-b934-527b5e6cb7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709353} {:answer/id #uuid "cfccc34c-66ed-5669-b586-5d6f2a740736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfccc34c-66ed-5669-b586-5d6f2a740736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709380} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da3e9d4-3fb8-5b72-85be-ee46f9ec95f7" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_L\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $L$ in $\\mathbb R^2$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cbe262a-5604-548c-8e08-b307475455a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709341} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0ecaf4-4f07-5e9c-9e98-b55a7c590ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cbe262a-5604-548c-8e08-b307475455a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709341} :answer-field/id #uuid "97cd7d6d-019d-5022-9afa-cd4440440fca" :answer-field/key "$-W_{\\gamma}+W_{\\alpha}+W_{\\beta}=0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "433a644c-48df-5a46-a197-f2d9e0f90318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709344} {:answer/id #uuid "da71a092-befb-5ed3-bc95-dc4f1e1fac76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da71a092-befb-5ed3-bc95-dc4f1e1fac76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709383} :answer-field/id #uuid "aee31538-b9ee-5ba5-99cc-fbbdcf851bd0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2531c0de-3675-5020-a1d7-8086e25537fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709337} {:answer/id #uuid "7136436a-0b13-5308-a59b-42f8db864321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2531c0de-3675-5020-a1d7-8086e25537fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709337} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6445d77-a620-50d4-9232-f3988b718f04" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "af4f9e55-d54c-55c6-a15a-c81c7ea7ab3f" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(2 - y\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(- x - 6 y - 1\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. The diagram shows three piecewise-smooth directed paths: $\\gamma$ goes from $B$ to $A$, $\\alpha$ goes from $C$ to $B$, $\\beta$ goes from $C$ to $A$.\n\n![gamma from B to A; alpha from C to B; beta from C to A](images/9a/9aee246533363494c0bc46bee33d742c79ed014a3c23599d5a5ebfd621801457.png)\n\nFor a directed path $\\eta$, write $W_\\eta=\\int_\\eta\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$. You are given $W_{\\alpha}=5$ and $W_{\\beta}=3$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Write $P=2 - y$ and $Q=- x - 6 y - 1$. The cross partials are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=-1\\\\Q_x&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThey agree everywhere. The components have continuous partial derivatives on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb R^2$, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative. For a conservative field with potential $f$, the fundamental theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=f(B)-f(A).\n$$\n\nFor such a conservative field, a closed path has the same endpoints, so its circulation is zero in either orientation. An open path can also have zero work when its endpoint potential values agree; zero work is not guaranteed for every open path. Follow the route $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$. Relative to the displayed arrows, its edge signs give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-W_{\\gamma}-W_{\\alpha}+W_{\\beta}&=0\\\\-W_{\\gamma}&=2\\\\W_{\\gamma}&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReversing an edge changes its work sign. The proposed cycle sum evaluates to $10$. Compare the proposed missing work with $-2$.\n\n- $-W_{\\gamma}+W_{\\alpha}+W_{\\beta}=0$. This is **false**.\n- $\\oint_L\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $L$ in $\\mathbb R^2$. This is **false**.\n- $\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative. This is **false**.\n- $W_{\\gamma}=0$. This is **false**.\n- None of the above This is **true**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2650ec76-d9aa-5866-b698-98a33c9516e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709339} {:answer/id #uuid "b17522d8-b416-572c-adfb-d9916f5ba946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b17522d8-b416-572c-adfb-d9916f5ba946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709374} :answer-field/id #uuid "683176a8-3a22-5b68-840e-aee3e496ff95" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_L\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $L$ in $\\mathbb R^2$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "260bd035-1c37-5aba-b0d8-16184752a0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709338} {:answer/id #uuid "3db7f22f-5ac4-5f92-b784-14a03b09e9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "260bd035-1c37-5aba-b0d8-16184752a0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709338} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c1f2ca-8b1f-5049-829f-3e1eb0e80322" :answer-field/key "$W_{\\beta}-W_{\\alpha}+W_{\\gamma}=0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e983892-4d75-5b40-9e5d-1dcec8c7da11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709335} {:answer/id #uuid "7d5d5078-fd85-5dc4-ba51-ec818ee7da7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e983892