/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c6f8647f-6810-515d-83be-4ca10e3c4503" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(3 y + 2\\right)\\mathbf i+\\left(3 x + 4 y - 1\\right)\\mathbf j\n$$\n\non $\\mathbb R^2$. The diagram shows three piecewise-smooth directed paths: $\\beta$ goes from $A$ to $B$, $\\alpha$ goes from $C$ to $B$, $\\gamma$ goes from $C$ to $A$.\n\n![beta from A to B; alpha from C to B; gamma from C to A](images/ca/ca9a13effdc9d90412cd0504a55ccbe4765c726ba2846d254abdcbd0d9a9628d.png)\n\nFor a directed path $\\eta$, write $W_\\eta=\\int_\\eta\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$. You are given $W_{\\alpha}=-4$ and $W_{\\gamma}=-6$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Write $P=3 y + 2$ and $Q=3 x + 4 y - 1$. The cross partials are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=3\\\\Q_x&=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThey agree everywhere. The components have continuous partial derivatives on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb R^2$, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative. For a conservative field with potential $f$, the fundamental theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=f(B)-f(A).\n$$\n\nFor such a conservative field, a closed path has the same endpoints, so its circulation is zero in either orientation. An open path can also have zero work when its endpoint potential values agree; zero work is not guaranteed for every open path. Follow the route $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$. Relative to the displayed arrows, its edge signs give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W_{\\beta}-W_{\\alpha}+W_{\\gamma}&=0\\\\W_{\\beta}&=2\\\\W_{\\beta}&=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReversing an edge changes its work sign. The proposed cycle sum evaluates to $0$. Compare the proposed missing work with $2$.\n\n- $\\oint_L\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $L$ in $\\mathbb R^2$. This is **false**.\n- $\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative. This is **false**.\n- $W_{\\beta}=2$. This is **true**.\n- $W_{\\beta}-W_{\\alpha}+W_{\\gamma}=0$. This is **true**.\n- None of the above This is **false**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709386 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4010b695-9844-5d0f-adf3-b6171b367297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709343} {:answer/id #uuid "d5984fa9-d32e-5d19-973f-a51fe95d77b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5984fa9-d32e-5d19-973f-a51fe95d77b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709382} :answer-field/id #uuid "18d870d5-9e7c-5905-bfdc-846cf4535465" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is **not** conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274319e2-f1e1-579d-af14-533c0a5e3210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709340} {:answer/id #uuid "48f34aca-c3e1-560b-8439-e72ad959b3f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "274319e2-f1e1-579d-af14-533c0a5e3210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709340} :answer-field/id #uuid "22738cdf-721f-5aa0-9bcf-647b6834fcd0" :answer-field/key "$\\oint_L\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\ne0$ for some closed path $L$ in $\\mathbb R^2$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709336} {:answer-field/choices [{: